{"id":"u-ede1d08a-67f7-4fb4-8b2e-e07e2ccea8c2","src":"community","title":"ChatGPT Supreme","author":"Kyle S.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/sCxPGi-boostcampweekaweekbprogram","desc":"This program is designed for people who want to build strength, muscle, and athletic durability without living in the gym.\n\nThe structure is built around five weekday morning workouts, with each session lasting approximately 45 minutes. It was specifically created for someone balancing resistance training with regular running and recreational sports, particularly soccer.\n\nThe goal is not to maximize any single fitness attribute. Instead, the focus is on becoming stronger, more muscular, better conditioned, and more resilient while maintaining a sustainable routine that can be followed for months or years.\n\nThe weekly structure prioritizes:\n\nUpper body strength and hypertrophy\nLower body strength and injury prevention\nCore development and trunk stability\nAthletic durability for running and field sports\nConsistent progression without excessive fatigue\n\nA rotating Week A / Week B format alternates the secondary upper-body emphasis between Push and Pull movements. This helps balance development, reduce overuse, and ensure all major muscle groups receive adequate attention over time.\n\nThe program is designed around commonly available equipment found in commercial gyms, including dumbbells, machines, cable stations, and Smith machines. No specialized equipment is required.\n\nRecovery is a core part of the design. Leg training is scheduled later in the week to accommodate Tuesday night soccer, while the midweek core and durability session provides additional work capacity, trunk strength, and injury prevention without compromising recovery for lower-body training.\n\nProgressive overload should be the primary driver of results. Focus on improving technique, increasing weight when appropriate, adding reps within the prescribed ranges, and maintaining consistency. Small improvements accumulated over time will produce far better results than constantly changing programs.\n\nThis is not a short-term challenge or a specialized peaking program. It is a practical, balanced training plan built for long-term success. Whether your goal is to look better, feel stronger, perform better on the field, or simply maintain an active lifestyle, this program provides a sustainable framework for continued progress.","level":["Beginner"],"goals":["Athletics","Muscle"],"equipment":["Garage Gym"],"minutes":50,"joins":0,"rate":0,"rateCount":1,"updated":"2026-06-09T11:49:24.977Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Push","Pull","Recovery/Core","Legs","Push Focus Upper"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Smith Machine)","sets":[{"r":6,"x":4}]},{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Seated Overhead Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Pec Deck (Machine)","sets":[{"r":12,"x":2}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"Tricep Rope Push Down (Cable)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"r":8,"x":4}]},{"n":"Chest Supported Row (Machine)","sets":[{"r":8,"x":4}]},{"n":"Single Arm Row (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Rear Delt Fly (Machine)","sets":[{"r":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"Hammer Curl (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Bicep Curl (EZ Bar)","sets":[{"r":12,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Knee Raise (Captain's Chair)","sets":[{"sec":720,"x":3}]},{"n":"Hanging Knee Raise","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Oblique Bend","sets":[{"sec":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"Decline Crunch (Weighted)","sets":[{"r":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"Abs Crunch (Machine)","sets":[{"r":15,"x":3}]},{"n":"Ab Wheel","sets":[{"r":12,"x":3}]},{"n":"Back Extension","sets":[{"r":12,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Squat (Smith Machine)","sets":[{"r":6,"x":4}]},{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":8,"x":4}]},{"n":"Leg Press","sets":[{"r":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Walking Lunge","sets":[{"r":12,"x":2}]},{"n":"Seated Hams